+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "toolChoice: 'required',",
+  "cause": "The refundAgent is configured with toolChoice 'required', which forces the model to call a tool on every turn, so after approveRefund is declined it cannot write a final reply and instead re-requests approval until the turn limit is hit.",
+  "evidence": "Running refundAgent against the real model with a declined approval reproduced the bug: every round finished with finishReason 'interrupted', empty text, and another approveRefund request for A-1001. After changing the setting to 'auto', the same run ended on the decline with finishReason 'stop' and the reply 'The refund for order A-1001 was not approved because it is a duplicate claim.'"
+}
